Chapter 1

1.1 Introduction

This project focuses on the design and development of a Tic-Tac-Toe game using the Java programming language.
The application is intended to provide users with an interactive and user-friendly gaming experience through a graphical user interface(GUI).
The game will allow users to play against another person or compete against a computer-controlled opponent.

The project aims to develop practical programming skills through the application of Java programming concepts.
These include constuctors, access modifiers, control statements, graphical user interfaces and object-oriented programming principles.

The application will also include additional features such as score tracking and different AI difficulty level.
Through this project, the group aims to demonstrate the software development process, from planning and design to implementation and testing.

1.2 Backround of the project

Tic-Tac-Toe is a traditional two player strategy game played on a grid, where players take turns placing their respective symbols, X and O.
The objective is to form a straight line of three matching symbols horizontally, vertically or diagonally before the opponent does.

With the development of computer technology, traditional games can be transformed into digital applications that provide interactive experiences.
Developing a Tic-Tac-Toe game using Java provides an opportunity to apply programming concepts while creating a practical application.

The proposed application will extend the traditional game by introducing a graphical interface, a computer-controlled opponent and score tracking.
These features are intended to make the game more engaging and provide users with different ways to play.

1.3 Project Rationale

The development of this Tic-Tac-Toe application is motivated by the need to make the traditional game more accessible and interactive.
Traditional Tic-Tac-Toe requires two people to participate, which can limit individuals who want to play when another player is unavailable.
Basic versions of the game may lack additional features such as different difficulty levels, score tracking.

This project therefore aims to enhance the traditional gaming experience by developing a Java based application that allows users to play against another person or a computer- controlled opponent.
Additional features will provide users with more playing options and create a more engaging gaming experience.

1.4 Aim and Objectives

1.4.1 Aim 

The aim of this project is to design and develop a functional, user-friendly Tic-Tac-Toe game using Java, incorporating both multiplayer and AI features.

1.4.2 Objectives

The objectives of the project are to:

Develop a user-friendly graphical interface for the Tic-Tac-Toe game.
Implement two player mode and player versus computer mode with different difficulty levels
Implement a scoring system to keep track of players' wins and losses.
Apply Java programming concepts, including constructors, access modifiers and control statements.
Test the application to ensure that it functions correctly and meets the project requirements.

1.5 Scope of the project

The project covers the design and implementation of a desktop-based Tic-Tac-Toe application using Netbeans and IntelliJ IDEA development environment.
The application will use a graphical user interface to allow users to access the different game features.

The system will support two-player gameplay and a single-player mode against an AI opponent. 
It will also include a scoring system to keep track of players' wins and losses.

The project will focus on the functionality, usability and reliability of the application.
It will cover the planning, design, implementation and testing stages of software development.

